From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:01:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, server: Read and set the placement of other
 processes' windows.

GetWindowPlacement() of a window of another process made up a placement
from the window rect, and SetWindowPlacement() failed.  On Windows both
work as for a window of the calling process: tools/ownerprobe in the
wine-altars repository shows the other process's view and the owning
process's own view line for line equal, and setting the normal position
from outside moves the window.

The placement a window's process keeps (the normal rect, the minimized
and maximized positions, WPF_RESTORETOMAXIMIZED) now goes to the
server whenever it changes, into the window's shared memory, and another
process reads it from there, updating it from where the window is now
as the owning process does when asked; no message is sent, so it works
for a thread that takes none, as it must for Wine's own test.  Setting
it goes to the window's thread as WM_WINE_SETWINDOWPLACEMENT, like
SetWindowPos() and ShowWindow() of another thread's window, in the DPI
of the thread that asked.

Windows also reports WPF_RESTORETOMAXIMIZED for a window as soon as it
is maximized, not only once it is minimized from there: the three
todo_wine in test_other_process_window() expected that, and pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

